{"step_index":56,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T07:42:54Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. 请接收数据获取蛋返回的上海温度结构化数据，将其渲染为友好的卡片 UI，突出展示上海当前温度及未来3天温度趋势。\n\n<summary>\n\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Core request (user, Chinese):** As the 展示蛋 (e3) module, receive the structured Shanghai temperature data returned by the data-fetching egg (e2) and render it as a friendly card UI highlighting (a) Shanghai's current temperature and (b) the 3-day temperature trend.\n- **Success criteria:** Working card UI in the e3 workspace showing Shanghai's current temp prominently + a 3-day trend with per-day high/low and a visual trend indicator.\n- **Constraints:** Source files only under `/home/administator/workspace/create_idea/worktrees/e1/e3`; dependency-free plain Node; preserve backward compatibility with existing tests; concise GitHub-markdown response with file:// links.\n- **Ambiguity resolved:** No Shanghai data existed in e3 originally, so the canonical source is sibling egg e2's `shanghai_weather.json`, copied into e3 as `data/shanghai.json`. The e2 schema differs from e3's card schema, so a mapping/normalization layer (`mapShanghaiData`) is required — not hand-editing sample.json, not hardcoding.\n\n## 2. Progress\n**Completed (verified by reading full files):**\n- `data/shanghai.json` present in e3 (60 lines, 1428 bytes) with full e2 schema.\n- `src/weather-card.js` (283 lines) contains: updated doc comment (lines 6–34) documenting `mapShanghaiData` and optional `daily` field; `WMO_CODE_MAP` (lines 84–95); `WMO_ZH` Chinese labels (lines 98–105); `codeToCondition(code)` (107–110); `round1(n)` (112–114); `extractTime(observedAt)` regex `/T(\\d{2}:\\d{2})/` (116–119); `WEEKDAY_ZH` (121); `weekdayOf(\n<truncated 2953 bytes>\nctStyles()` only reads it at runtime).\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- No browser needed; module emits HTML strings; tests run in plain Node (v24.21.0, `package.json` `\"type\": \"module\"`).\n- Working assumption: e2's `shanghai_weather.json` is canonical; copied into e3 (`data/shanghai.json`) to keep e3 self-contained and testable.\n- `weekdayOf` uses `new Date(y, m-1, d)` — for 2026-10-24 that's a Friday (五); 2026-10-25 Saturday (六); 2026-10-26 Sunday (日). Labels: today = 今天, tomorrow = 明天, else weekday char.\n- Dependencies: `mapShanghaiData` depends on `codeToCondition`/`WMO_ZH`/`weekdayOf` (all written). `dailyRow` depends on `resolveCondition` (written).\n\n## 5. Next Steps\n1. **Fix `esc()` bug:** insert `function esc(v) {` before line 128 in `src/weather-card.js`.\n2. **Add `export function mapShanghaiData(raw)`** after `hourlyRow` (line 183), before `renderWeatherCard` (line 185), per conversion spec.\n3. **Add `dailyRow(daily, unit)`** (internal function, used by card): renders `.wc-daily` block — for each day: label, condition icon (via `resolveCondition`), high/low, and a visual trend indicator (▲/▼/→ arrow vs previous day's high, plus a CSS bar scaled by temp). Append `.wc-daily` CSS to `CARD_CSS`.\n4. **Update `renderWeatherCard`:** insert `dailyHtml = dailyRow(city.daily, unit)` after stats, before hourly.\n5. **Update `index.html`:** import `../data/shanghai.json` + `mapShanghaiData`; call `renderWeatherGridToElement(document.getElementById('weather'), [mapShanghaiData(shanghai)])`; change title/hero text to 上海天气.\n6. **Add tests** in `test/weather-card.test.js`: mapper (temp 20.7, humidity 87, time \"15:15\", condition 'drizzle', windKmh 54.7, daily length 3 with correct high/low), daily row (3 days present, high/low values, day labels).\n7. **Run** `node test/weather-card.test.js` from e3; verify all pass.\n8. **Verify** rendered HTML via quick node scrip\n---\nThe checkpoint summary has been truncated due to hitting max length. Please see the conversation log file for the full conversation.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
